## ROOT CAUSE
The closure made structured `requestIntent` tier 1 and the lexicon tier 2 but wired the veto asymmetrically (`read` outranks the lexicon, `other` does not) — on exactly the turns the prompt labels `other`, the lexicon is again the sole decider. The lifecycle gate checks lead words and model *fields*, not the model's *classification* or sentence mood. Same shape #56 named: a regex standing in for structured intent.

## SYSTEMIC IMPACT
Every non-mutation Brain Chat turn containing *hire/fire/merge/split/approve/reject/archive/remove/invite/enable/promote/reopen…* as noun or verb, when the model classifies it `other`, gets a non-sequitur receipt instead of its answer. Reversible-and-visible wrong-entity archive on bare-name collisions (D2). No fabrication ships through any shape I could construct when the model classifies the request; the lexicon-only tier ships 33.6 % of my generator when it does not.

